    doc+='<section id="result"><p class="'+('status' if accepted else 'unknown')+'">'+esc(proof_status)+'. Every recorded point tree and native outcome, including unknowns, passed independent reconstruction/replay.</p><p>'+math(base['case']['target'])+'</p><p>In words: adding to a successor on the left gives the successor of the corresponding sum. The exact input theory is unchanged from the earlier zero-left experiment: '+math(base['case']['theory']['axioms']['AZ'])+' and '+math(base['case']['theory']['axioms']['AS'])+', with the natural-number induction schema enabled. The target is absent from the axioms. This is a recursive-addition fragment, not all Peano arithmetic.</p><div class="metrics"><div><strong>159</strong>complete five-node terms</div><div><strong>39 / 48</strong>retained inference interfaces</div><div><strong>24</strong>fully native-admitted union definitions</div><div><strong>'+str(len(found))+'</strong>searched candidate observations</div></div></section>'
    doc+='<section id="grammar"><h2>The entire declared grammar is preserved</h2><p>Generic infrastructure enumerates every term through five syntax nodes, every recursive-equation direction, expression occurrence and missing-variable substitution; both target-variable induction alternatives; explicit conditional step contexts; and every contextual generalization. No target-proof sequence is supplied. The zero-left lane adds the actual previously searched, completely native-checked theorem as a closed reusable proof, never a new axiom. Its one-edge applications have two explicit inputs: the current equality and the proved universal theorem. The authored local interfaces are not called learned.</p>'+table(['Inventory','Terms','Formula basis','Full interfaces','Full local definitions','Exposed instantiations','Exposed induction instances'],[(s['lane'],s['terms'],s['basis_formulas'],s['interfaces'],s['local_definitions'],s['primitive_counts']['instantiate'],s['primitive_counts']['induction']) for s in prep['variants']])+'<p>The two complete primitive diagnostic streams total '+number(sum(s['primitive_uncompressed_bytes'] for s in prep['variants']))+' uncompressed bytes. Every instance was independently reconstructed. These streams are exposed preparation catalogs, remain natively unadmitted, and are not the searched contextual grammar. There are no admissible exposed quantifier-distribution instances because both declared variables occur in each relevant antecedent; guarded distribution does occur inside the fully checked generic induction interfaces.</p></section>'
    doc+='<section id="pruning"><h2>Proved structural pruning before admission</h2><p>All full-grammar templates, including native-unresolved ones, enter a least fixed point from every zero-input output. A rule is removed only when at least one premise is outside that closed set. Induction over strict-prior proof positions proves that no finite full-grammar proof word can contain such a rule. Conditional assumptions remain explicit inside implication formulas. The certificate stores every full edge, every formula rank/layer and each removed rule’s unreachable premise; an independent priority worklist reconstructs them all.</p><p>This is authored graph analysis, not a learned failure marking. It preserves all successful finite proof words in this grammar and makes no claim about unrestricted first-order nonprovability. It also computes bounded syntactic derivability; GCTS subsequently assembles actual placements and source-explicit proof words. It selects no target-proof path or preferred induction variable.</p>'+table(['Inventory','Full → retained interfaces','Full → retained definitions','Reachable formulas','Closure layers','12-row placements, full → retained'],[(s['lane'],str(s['full_interfaces'])+' → '+str(s['retained_interfaces']),str(s['full_definitions'])+' → '+str(s['retained_definitions']),s['reachable_formulas'],s['rounds']+1,str(p['prospective_point_counts'][0]['placements'])+' → '+str(s['point_counts'][0]['placements'])) for s,p in zip(pruning['variants'],prep['variants'])])+'<p>All 17 no-transfer definitions are byte-identical members of the 24-definition union. Only this complete retained union is admitted natively; the full unpruned catalogs remain available. <a href="finite-inventory-pruning.html">Read the safety lemma and scope</a>.</p></section>'
    doc+='<section id="search"><h2>What the automatic point search did</h2><p>Four fresh models use the frozen complete frontier graph: global dead ends, then global forced moves, then earliest generation, with complete fallback and exact rollback. Every required C/G/I1/I2 point starts at generation zero; occupancy and extended scalar catalog markings are exact, with fixed orientation. Every retained interface and strict-prior source alternative is generated. Two repetitions per inventory preserve the same inventory; the without/with-transfer inventories differ semantically and do not provide an equal-inventory search-speed comparison. No RL policy was trained.</p>'+table(['Run','Point outcome','Attempts','Search seconds','Model seconds','Placements'],[(o['id'],o['status'],o['attempts'],sec(o['search_seconds']),sec(o['model_setup_seconds']),o['placements']) for o in search['observations']])+'</section>'
