    doc+='<section id="validation"><h2>Whole checking of the automatically selected certificate</h2><p>Each complete point trace is checkpointed before validation. The original selected request contains all actually used local definitions. A generic expansion maps those local assumptions to their actual earlier sources, then exact-formula DAG sharing and dependency slicing produce a primitive certificate. Both versions retain the byte-identical original theory and target and add no theorem-specific inference. Exact repeat validation requests may reuse an earlier completed native result; historical time is shown below, and fresh verification cost is counted only once.</p>'+table(['Run','Whole variant','Commands','Native outcome','Exact cached request','Historical native seconds'],variants)+'</section>'
