    doc+='<section id="costs"><h2>Preparation and verification dominate the cost</h2>'+table(['Component','Seconds','Peak RSS bytes'],[(a,sec(b),c) for a,b,c in cost_rows])+'<p class="unknown">The first local-compaction audit hit its declared 512 MiB RSS ceiling while retaining both inventory graphs. Its exact source freeze, plan and log are preserved. That version failed to checkpoint elapsed time/peak RSS on its exception, so both remain unknown. Attempt 2 changed only graph lifetime and exception checkpoints, retaining the same 180-second and 512 MiB ceilings, and passed. No native rejection or theorem-search failure is inferred from this preparation unknown.</p><p>Unique native producer computations total '+sec(native_cost)+' s / '+number(native_steps)+' microsteps across '+str(len(pilot_records)+len(admission_records)+len(records)+len(forward_records))+' queries. Four accepted byte-identical pilot requests are credited as historical admission, not repeated fresh cost. The original zero-left theorem’s preparation and 92-query certification history remains in <a href="induction_receptors.html#costs">its separate complete ledger</a>, and is not treated as free. Native pilot replay and later admissions overlapped on the shared host; component sums are not a single invented end-to-end wall time. Manual infrastructure development and the first failed compaction-audit time are unmeasured.</p><p>The setup/native checker cost motivates the proved full-grammar pruning: '+str(sum(s['full_definitions'] for s in pruning['variants']))+' authored local definitions become 24 unique reachable definitions to admit. This measured structural reduction is useful; it is not evidence of RL progress or superiority over existing automated theorem provers.</p>'
